{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Method on Validator<D>.\n/// Load this criterion's evidence and decode its answer as V::Ok.\n/// Ok(None) means no saved record exists.\npub fn load_evidence<V: Criterion<D>>(\n    &self,\n    criterion: &V,\n) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Fingerprinted<D, V::Ok>>, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n```\n\n`load_evidence` captures the source identity and criterion path while constructing\nits future. It retains no reference to the criterion value while storage is\npending, so the criterion needs no `Sync` bound. It loads the complete record and\ndecodes its output under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`.\nRevision and input comparison are separate steps.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `check_node`.\n\n- **Missing record returns `Ok(None)`.** `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` loads before any store and asserts `is_none()`. It also does this after `verify` without a store. `review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk` and `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` do the same.\n- **Source identity and criterion path select the record.**\n  - `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` loads with a different criterion path (`new`) and with a different source node (`Node(2)`). Both return `None`.\n  - `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` loads node 8 and gets `None`.\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` loads the `text` path before it is stored and gets `None`.\n- **The complete record is loaded and the output decoded.** `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts the loaded output, source node, criterion path, revision and dependencies all equal the stored values. `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another` and `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` assert that loaded dependencies equal the saved ones. `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` does the same for edge dependencies.\n- **Decode failures return `ValidationError::Output`, including for stale records.**\n  - `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` loads a stale record with a changed revision (`v2`) and with changed dependencies. Both return `Output` and perform no reads.\n  - `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` stores an output of the wrong type with an obsolete revision. It asserts `Output` and that the file is unchanged.\n- **Malformed stored records and storage failures return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n  - The malformed-record test writes \"not JSON\" and asserts `Graph(FileStorageError::Json)`.\n  - `loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers` and `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` set `fail_load` and assert `Graph(\"load\")`.\n- **Revision and input comparison are separate steps.**\n  - `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` loads a `v1` record when asked for `v2`.\n  - It then confirms `procedure_matches` is false, so the caller does the comparison.\n  - `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` loads successfully while reads and edges fail. Only `check_inputs` reports the error.\n  - `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` loads a record whose revision differs from the criterion's.\n- **No `Sync` bound and no retained criterion reference.** In `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync`, `send(validator.load_evidence(&descriptor))` requires the future to be `Send`. `Review` contains `Cell` fields (`descriptor_reads` and a `Cell` answer), so it is `Send` but not `Sync`. A future holding `&Review` would therefore fail to compile.\n- **Signature and typed return.** The same test, together with the typed loads elsewhere, exercises the `Result<Option<Fingerprinted<...>>>` form.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
